# Project Organization & File Placement Standards

## **MANDATORY: No Test-Related Files in Root Directory**

**CRITICAL**: ALL test-related files (documentation, scripts, output files, SQL scripts, PowerShell scripts, etc.) MUST be placed in the `QA Tests/` directory, NOT in the project root.

**Why This Matters:**
- ✅ **Organization**: Keeps the root directory clean and focused on essential project files
- ✅ **Maintainability**: Centralizes all test-related content in a predictable location
- ✅ **Discoverability**: All test files are in one place
- ✅ **Version Control**: Reduces clutter in git status and root folder listings

---

## Root Directory - Allowed Files ONLY

The root directory should ONLY contain:

### ✅ **Allowed in Root:**
- `README.md` - Project overview and getting started guide
- `CHANGELOG.md` - Version history and release notes
- `LICENSE.md` - Project license information
- `.gitignore` - Git ignore rules
- `.gitmodules` - Git submodules configuration
- `package.json` / `package-lock.json` - Node.js dependencies (for Playwright)
- `playwright.config.ts` - Playwright configuration
- Solution files (`.sln`)
- Project configuration files that MUST be at root level

### ❌ **NOT Allowed in Root (Move to QA Tests/):**

| File Type | Example Files | Correct Location |
|-----------|---------------|------------------|
| Test SQL scripts | `assign-test-roles.sql`, `create-test-users.sql`, `setup-test-data.sql`, `check-*.sql`, `verify-*.sql` | `QA Tests/Scripts/` |
| Test PowerShell scripts | `create-test-data.ps1`, `setup-database-*.ps1`, `verify-*.ps1` | `QA Tests/Scripts/` |
| Build output files | `build-output.txt`, `test-results.txt` | `QA Tests/Test Execution Results/` |
| Test documentation | `*_SUMMARY.md`, `*_COMPLETE.md`, `*_REPORT.md`, `PR_DESCRIPTION.md` | `QA Tests/Documentation/` |
| Session summaries | `SESSION_*.md`, `PHASE_*.md` | `QA Tests/Documentation/` |
| Test plans | `*_PLAN.md`, `*_STRATEGY.md` | `QA Tests/Test Plans/` |
| Coverage reports | `*_COVERAGE*.md` | `QA Tests/Summary Reports/` |

---

## QA Tests Directory Structure

All test-related files MUST go in the appropriate subdirectory:

```
QA Tests/
├── Scripts/                      # SQL and PowerShell test scripts
│   ├── assign-test-roles.sql     ✅ Test role setup
│   ├── create-test-users.sql     ✅ Test user creation
│   ├── setup-test-data.sql       ✅ Test data seeding
│   ├── setup-database.ps1        ✅ Database setup scripts
│   └── verify-*.ps1              ✅ Verification scripts
├── Documentation/                # General test documentation
│   ├── SETUP_GUIDE.md            ✅ Setup instructions
│   ├── PR_DESCRIPTION.md         ✅ PR descriptions
│   └── SESSION_SUMMARY.md        ✅ Session summaries
├── Test Execution Results/       # Output from test runs
│   ├── build-output.txt          ✅ Build logs
│   ├── test-results.txt          ✅ Test output
│   └── *.trx                     ✅ Test result files
├── Playwright Tests/             # Playwright E2E tests
├── C# Tests/                     # C# unit/integration tests
├── Integration Tests/            # Integration test suites
├── Summary Reports/              # Coverage and summary reports
└── Test Plans/                   # Test planning documents
```

